                <pb facs="0566" n="556" sameAs="frus:frus1948v07/pg556"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/11–948: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-11-09">November 9,
                        1948</date>.<lb/>[Received November 9—12:43 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>539. <hi rendition="#italic">Sheng Tang Shih Pao</hi> today states North China
                    People’s Government established September 20 with Tung Pi-wu [as] Chairman and
                    Pu I-po, Lan Kung-wu and Yang Hsiu-feng [as] first, second and third vice
                    chairman respectively. Other heads of Government Lan Kung-wu, Minister Interior;
                    Chao Chieh-fu, Minister Education; Jung Tse-ho, Minister Finance; Yao I-lin,
                    Minister Industry and Commerce; Sung Shao-wen, Minister Agriculture; Huang
                    Ching, Minister State Enterprises; Wu Ching-tien, Minister Communications; Yin
                    Hsih-peng, Minister Health; Hsu Chien-kuo, Minister Security; Hsieh Chueh-tsai,
                    Minister Justice. November 2 will henceforth be celebrated in northeast as
                    Victory Day.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 672, repeated Department 539, Tientsin 179, Peiping 264.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
